Changes in version 1.21.x

NEW FEATURES

+ plotHeatmap: heatmap of features by samples straight from a TreeSE, as a
  ggplot2 object, with row and column facets from rowData/colData and an
  optional row tree
+ plotDissimilarity: heatmap of a dissimilarity matrix between samples
+ getHeatmapOrder and sort.method (in plotHeatmap and plotDissimilarity):
  sort the rows and columns of heatmaps
+ plotOrdination for ordinations stored in reducedDims
+ Joint-RPCA visualisations: plotJointRPCA, plotJointRPCACovariance,
  plotJointRPCAExplainedVariance and plotJointRPCANetwork
+ plotRowTree, plotColTree: heatmap.by shows per-taxon values as a heatmap
  or as rings next to the tree tips
+ plotSeries: each feature is drawn as its own line, as in matplot(), also
  without colour.by
+ plotBoxplot: outlier.size, outlier.colour, outlier.alpha and outlier.shape
  style the boxplot outliers (shown with add.points = FALSE). The help page
  now lists all customisation arguments, grouped by plot layer
+ New example datasets in multimedia_data_demo: se_relative, tse_relative and
  tse_pathway

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

+ plotRDA, plotCCA: the vectors are scaled by a common factor so that the
  longest one reaches 75% of the extent of the samples (as in vegan
  biplots), instead of crowding at the origin. Their relative lengths and
  directions are unchanged; vec.scale = FALSE draws them at the original
  length, and a number sets the multiplier
+ Colour-blind-friendly colours by default: discrete variables are coloured
  with the Okabe-Ito palette for up to 9 groups (black is used only for the
  9th) and with viridis for more, instead of the Tableau palette
+ A palette set with options(ggplot2.discrete.colour = ...) or
  options(ggplot2.discrete.fill = ...) is used in all plots, so one palette
  can be chosen for every figure, e.g. the earlier Tableau palette
  (see ?"mia-plot-args")
+ More readable default labels:
  - plotHeatmap and plotJointRPCACovariance draw column labels vertically
  - plotOrdination titles the axes by the method and component, e.g.
    "MDS1 (23.4%)" instead of "MDS_bray1"
  - plotLoadings shows the components in their order (PC2 before PC10),
    names unnamed components "Component 1", ..., titles the value axis
    "Loading" and leaves out the sign legend when all loadings have the
    same sign
  - Prevalence plots title their axes "Detection threshold (<assay>)",
    "Number of features" and "Mean relative abundance"
  - plotBoxplot facets (facet.by = "rownames") follow the order of
    'features', and plotMediation forest panels the order of the components
  - plotJointRPCANetwork keeps labels off the nodes
+ plotMediation heatmap: each tile shows the effect estimate with its
  significance, the colours use the colour-blind-safe red-blue palette and
  the panel is grey, so that small ACME effects stay visible on the shared
  colour scale. add.estimate = FALSE shows only the significance, and
  add.significance = "numeric" shows "p=0.012" or "p<0.001"
+ plotForest: confidence intervals from 'err.var' use the degrees of freedom
  given with the new 'df.var' or 'df' arguments; without them, the normal
  distribution is used with a warning. Earlier, the number of columns of the
  results table was used as the degrees of freedom

DEPRECATED AND DEFUNCT

+ plotPrevalence, plotRowPrevalence, plotPrevalentAbundance: as.relative and
  as_relative are deprecated. Calculate relative abundances with
  transformAssay(x, method = "relabundance") and use
  assay.type = "relabundance" instead
+ getNeatOrder is deprecated; use getHeatmapOrder
+ plotTaxaPrevalence and plotFeaturePrevalence are removed (deprecated since
  2025); use plotRowPrevalence
+ plotBoxplot: the misspelled argument add.chance is renamed to add.change

BUG FIXES

+ Legend titles of coloured or filled variables (colour.by, fill.by, ...)
  can be changed with labs(), e.g. + labs(colour = "Sample type"); the
  title was set as the scale name, which labs() cannot override
+ plotOrdination: the explained variance shown in the axis titles is the
  percentage of the total variance for ordinations that store eigenvalues
  (e.g. MDS); earlier the eigenvalues were multiplied by 100
+ plotOrdination: aspect.ratio = "eigen" now scales the panel by the explained
  variance (it had no effect); the documentation named a non-existent
  panel.by.eigen argument
+ plotBoxplot: significance brackets no longer run through boxes or each
  other, and hide.ns = TRUE stacks the shown brackets without gaps
+ plotBoxplot: paired lines follow the time order with more than two time
  points
+ plotBoxplot: variables named "x", "y" or "df" work
+ plotRowPrevalence: count thresholds are no longer multiplied by 100
+ plotHeatmap, plotDissimilarity: labs(fill = ...) sets the legend title
+ plotHeatmap: facetting rows and columns by variables with the same name
  works
+ plotRDA, plotCCA: samples left out of the ordination (e.g. with
  na.action = na.exclude) no longer add an empty "NA" legend entry
+ plotAbundance: rows named in the new other.name argument (default
  "Other", e.g. the group from subsetBy(collapse = TRUE)) are shown last in
  the bars and legend instead of among the features; other.name = NULL
  turns this off
+ plotAbundance: a row named "Other" (e.g. from subsetBy(collapse = TRUE))
  is shown last in the bars and legend instead of among the features
+ plotForest: labels use two decimals for the CI ("-0.45 (-1.59, 0.70)")
  and show p-values below 0.001 as "<0.001" instead of "0"
+ plotRowGraph, plotPrevalentAbundance: points are coloured correctly when
  both colour.by and shape.by are given

MINOR NOTES

+ Requires mia (>= 1.21.31), whose subsetBy() is used in examples and tests
+ plotBoxplot: variable names that clash with internal columns
  (e.g. "x_point") give an error instead of being silently overwritten
+ plotBoxplot: step.increase is applied once (it was applied twice) and is
  measured from the highest group a bracket spans; other arguments are
  passed to ggpubr::stat_pvalue_manual
+ plotSeries: legends keyed by rownames follow the order of rownames(x), and
  colour.lab also titles the line type and size legends when they use the
  same variable
+ plotOrdination, plotBoxplot: size.by titles the size legend
+ plotPrevalence, plotRowPrevalence: until removed, as.relative works as
  documented (earlier only as_relative did)
+ The pkgdown reference page groups the functions into categories
